# Always push after commit

After a successful commit you were asked to make, or when shipping a completed fix, push to the tracked remote (`git push -u origin HEAD`).

- Never force-push `main` or `master`.
- Do not push broken, secret-laden, or incomplete work.
- Do not skip hooks. Do not amend a pushed commit.
- If push fails on auth, report the exact error; do not claim it succeeded.
